  <exercise number="223" has_solution="true">
    <problem>
      <p>Find the tangential and normal acceleration components with the position vector $$\mathbf{\text{r}}(t) = \left\langle {\text{cos}\mspace{2mu} t,\text{sin}\mspace{2mu} t,e^{t}} \right\rangle.$$</p>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <p>$$a_{T} = \frac{e^{2t}}{\sqrt{1 + e^{2t}}},$$ $$a_{N} = \frac{\sqrt{2e^{2t} + 4e^{2t}\text{sin}\mspace{2mu} t\mspace{2mu}\text{cos}\mspace{2mu} t + 1}}{\sqrt{1 + e^{2t}}}$$</p>
    </solution>
  </exercise>
